     <!--#include virtual="/php/suttasidebar.html" --> 

  <div id="sutta">
  
    <h4 id="thig5.4" class="h1">Thig 5:4  Nandā’s Vision</h4>
          <div class="verse">
            <p>“Sick, putrid, unclean:</p>
            <p>look, Nandā, at this physical heap.</p>
            <p>Through contemplation of the foul,</p>
            <p>develop your mind,</p>
            <p>make it one, well-centered.</p>
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p class="v2">As this [your body], so that.</p>
              <p class="v2">As that, so this.</p>
              <p>It gives off a foul stench,</p>
              <p>the delight of fools.”</p>
              <p>Considering it thus,</p>
              <p>untiring, both day &amp; night,</p>
              <p>I, with my own discernment</p>
              <p class="v2">dissecting it,</p>
              <p class="v4">saw.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p>And as I, heedful,</p>
              <p class="v2">examined it aptly,</p>
              <p><em>this</em> body—as it actually is—</p>
              <p>was seen inside &amp; out.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p>Then was I disenchanted with the body</p>
              <p class="v2">&amp; dispassionate within:</p>
              <p>Heedful, detached,</p>
              <p class="v2">calmed was I.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p class="v4">Unbound.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
          </div><!--end verse-->
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
    </div><!--end:content-->
    
